  (2, 'Synovial joints, ligaments, cartilage and tendons', 'Which bones articulate at the elbow joint?', 'Pelvis and the femur', 'Humerus and scapula', 'Humerus, radius, ulna', 'Femur and tibia only', 'C', 'The elbow is a hinge joint. The knee is femur and tibia, the shoulder is humerus and scapula, and the hip is pelvis and femur.', 'foundation', 'recall', 'AO1'),
  (3, 'Synovial joints, ligaments, cartilage and tendons', 'What is the role of cartilage at a joint?', 'It attaches muscle to bone', 'It cushions the ends of bones', 'It attaches bone to bone', 'It produces red blood cells', 'B', 'Tendons attach muscle to bone and ligaments attach bone to bone.', 'foundation', 'recall', 'AO1'),
