  (1, 'Principles of training and FITT', 'A swimmer trains mainly by swimming rather than running. Which principle of training is this?', 'Specificity', 'Overload', 'Progression', 'Reversibility', 'A', 'Specificity means matching training to the needs and movements of the activity.', 'foundation', 'applied', 'AO2'),
  (2, 'Types of training', 'What is circuit training?', 'Changing speed and terrain during a run', 'Lifting a very heavy weight just once', 'Exercises at stations with short rests', 'Running at a steady pace for a long time', 'C', 'Circuits can be designed to improve different components of fitness. Steady running is continuous training and changing speed is fartlek.', 'foundation', 'recall', 'AO1'),
  (3, 'Warm up and cool down', 'Jogging slowly to raise the heart rate is which part of a warm up?', 'Skill rehearsal', 'Mobility', 'Pulse raising', 'Stretching', 'C', 'A warm up includes pulse raising, mobility, stretching, dynamic movements and skill rehearsal.', 'foundation', 'applied', 'AO2'),
