from (values
  (1, 'Skilful movement and classification of skills', 'Which is a characteristic of skilful movement?', 'It is made up differently each time', 'It always needs maximum effort', 'It is efficient, with no wasted energy', 'It is hesitant and jerky', 'C', 'J587 lists the characteristics of skilful movement as efficient, pre-determined, co-ordinated, fluent and aesthetic.', 'foundation', 'recall', 'AO1'),
  (2, 'Skilful movement and classification of skills', 'What does it mean to say a skilful movement is pre-determined?', 'The performer knows the aim before starting', 'The result is decided by the referee in advance', 'The movement is copied from a coach every time', 'The movement only ever happens by accident', 'A', 'A skilled performer has a clear goal for the movement and performs it to achieve that goal.', 'higher', 'recall', 'AO1'),
  (3, 'Skilful movement and classification of skills', 'Which is the best example of a closed skill?', 'Dribbling past a defender', 'Returning a serve in tennis', 'A gymnast performing a vault', 'A pass during a football match', 'C', 'Closed skills happen in a stable, predictable environment. The others depend on what opponents do, so they are open.', 'foundation', 'applied', 'AO2'),
  (4, 'Skilful movement and classification of skills', 'Which is the best example of a complex skill?', 'Swimming one length of front crawl', 'Walking slowly to the start line', 'Jogging at a steady, even pace', 'Choosing a shot in a tennis rally', 'D', 'Complex skills need lots of decisions and attention. Simple skills need little thought.', 'foundation', 'applied', 'AO2'),
  (5, 'Skilful movement and classification of skills', 'Why is a penalty in football often placed towards the closed end of the environmental continuum?', 'It needs many decisions to be made quickly', 'The environment is stable and predictable', 'It uses a large number of muscle groups', 'It is performed as part of a whole team', 'B', 'There are no moving opponents apart from the goalkeeper, so the taker can perform the same way each time. Decisions relate to the difficulty continuum, not the environmental one.', 'higher', 'applied', 'AO3'),
  (6, 'Goal setting and SMART targets', 'In the J587 version of SMART goal setting, what does the R stand for?', 'Recorded', 'Relevant', 'Rewarded', 'Realistic', 'A', 'J587 uses Specific, Measurable, Achievable, Recorded, Timed. Other versions use Realistic, so read the question carefully.', 'foundation', 'recall', 'AO1'),
  (7, 'Goal setting and SMART targets', 'How can goal setting help a performer?', 'It means that they no longer need to warm up', 'It removes the need for any feedback at all', 'It can motivate them to keep training', 'It guarantees that they will win every time', 'C', 'Goals are used for exercise and training adherence, to motivate performers and to improve or optimise performance.', 'foundation', 'recall', 'AO1'),
  (8, 'Guidance and feedback', 'A swimming teacher gives a beginner a float to hold. Which type of guidance is this?', 'Visual', 'Mechanical', 'Verbal', 'Manual', 'B', 'Mechanical guidance uses equipment or aids. Manual guidance is when the coach physically moves or supports the performer.', 'foundation', 'applied', 'AO2'),
  (9, 'Guidance and feedback', 'What is knowledge of performance?', 'Feedback a performer gives to their coach', 'Feedback about the final score or outcome', 'Feedback on the quality of technique', 'Feedback shouted from the crowd', 'C', 'Knowledge of results is about the outcome; knowledge of performance is about how well the movement was performed.', 'foundation', 'recall', 'AO1'),
  (10, 'Mental preparation', 'Before competing, a gymnast pictures a calm, relaxing place in their mind. Which technique is this?', 'Imagery', 'Manual guidance', 'Knowledge of results', 'Selective attention', 'A', 'Imagery is creating pictures in the mind, for example to relax. Mental rehearsal is picturing performing the skill itself.', 'foundation', 'applied', 'AO2'),
  (11, 'Mental preparation', 'What is mental rehearsal?', 'Being physically guided through a movement', 'Picturing performing a skill, without moving', 'Watching a demonstration given by a coach', 'Practising a skill many times on the pitch', 'B', 'Mental rehearsal builds confidence and helps performers prepare the movement in their mind.', 'foundation', 'recall', 'AO1'),
  (12, 'Mental preparation', 'What is selective attention?', 'Listening carefully to all advice from the crowd', 'Watching every player on the pitch at once', 'Choosing which training sessions to attend', 'Focusing on key cues and ignoring distractions', 'D', 'For example, a cricketer focuses on the ball and ignores crowd noise.', 'foundation', 'recall', 'AO1'),
  (13, 'Mental preparation', 'Before serving, a tennis player says to themselves, "I''ve practised this, I can win this point." Which technique is this?', 'Extrinsic feedback', 'Imagery', 'Positive thinking', 'Mechanical guidance', 'C', 'Positive thinking, or positive self-talk, increases confidence and reduces worry.', 'foundation', 'applied', 'AO2')
